Package: zuxlsx
Title: Read 'xlsx' Workbooks Without System Dependencies
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Pedro", "Baltazar", , "pedrobtz@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Brecht", "Sanders", role = "cph",
           comment = "xlsxio, bundled in src/vendor/xlsxio"))
Description: Reads spreadsheet data from 'xlsx' workbooks using a bundled
    copy of the 'xlsxio' reader (<https://github.com/brechtsanders/xlsxio>),
    so that no system XML or ZIP library is required. The 'Expat' parser and
    the 'miniz' ZIP reader are linked statically at install time from the
    'zuxml' and 'zukomp' packages, which means there is no run-time
    dependency on either of them. Worksheets are read as a stream, so a
    workbook does not have to be held in memory in full. Writing workbooks
    is out of scope.
